<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n73721" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁμοκλ-άω</span></b> , 
			Ep.
		
		impf.
		3pl.
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁμόκλεον</span> (as if from <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁμοκλ-κλέω</span></b> , cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁμοκλεῖ: ἀπειλεῖ, βοᾷ,</span>
		<i><span class="en">
			Hsch.
		</span></i>) and 3sg.
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁμόκλᾱ</span> (v. infr.) : aor.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁμόκλησα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hom.
				</span></i>
			 (v. infr.), <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>El.</u>
				712
			</span></i> ; 
				Ion.
			 Iterat. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁμοκλήσασκε</span> (v.
			infr.) :—
				Ep.
			 Verb, <i>call</i> or <i>shout to,</i> c. dat., either
			to <i>encourage,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁμόκλεον ἀλλήλοισι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					15.658
				</span></i>
			 : once in Trag., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἵπποις ὁμοκλήσαντες</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>El.</u>
					712
				</span></i>
			 ; or (more freq.), to <i>upbraid, threaten,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δεινὰ ὁμοκλήσας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					5.439
				</span></i>
			, etc. ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁμοκλήσας ἔπος ηὔδα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					6.54
				</span></i>
			, etc. ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μέγα δὲ Τρώεσσιν ὁμόκλα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					18.156
				</span></i>
			 ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁ δ᾽ υἱάσιν οἷσιν ὁμόκλα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					24.248
				</span></i>
			 ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μνηστῆρες δ᾽ ἄρα πάντες ὁμόκλεον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					21.360
				</span></i>
			 : also c. dat. modi, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁμοκλήσασκέ τε μύθῳ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					2.199
				</span></i>
			 ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁμόκλησάν τ᾽ ἐπέεσσιν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					23.363
				</span></i>
			 : c. inf., <i>command loudly, call on</i> one
				<i>to</i> do, <i><span class="en">
				16.714
			</span></i>. (Spir. asp. indicated by 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κέκλεθ᾽ ὁμοκλήσας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					20.365
				</span></i>
			 (
				v.l.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κέκλετ᾽ ὀμ-</span>
			), spir. lenis by 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑπ᾽ ὀμοκλῆς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hes.
					<u>Sc.</u>
					341
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				<u>h.Cer.</u>
				88
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Call.
				<u>Del.</u>
				158
			</span></i> : the former is perh. due to the mistaken idea of connexion
			with <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁμός.</span>)</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
